"When you want to print an outgoing picking in an Italian company,\n"
"it will print you the DDT instead.  It is like the delivery\n"
"slip, but it also contains the value of the product,\n"
"the transportation reason, the carrier, ... which make it a DDT.\n"
"\n"
"We also use a separate sequence for the DDT as the number should not\n"
"have any gaps and should only be applied at the moment the goods are sent.\n"
"\n"
"When invoices are related to their sale order and the sale order with the\n"
"delivery, the system will automatically calculate the linked DDTs for every\n"
"invoice line to export in the FatturaPA XML.\n"

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_asset_ledger_document_compliance
msgid ""
"\n"
"Documents - Asset Compliance Reporting\n"
"======================================\n"
"\n"
"Compliance reporting over asset documents.\n"
"\n"
"* ``asset.compliance.report`` -- documents held versus required, valid,\n"
"  expired, expiring and missing counts, compliance percentage, next expiry and\n"
"  last verification date, per asset\n"
"* status classification: compliant, partial, non-compliant\n"
"* list, kanban, pivot and graph views, filtered by asset type, compliance\n"
"  status and expiration state\n"
"* read by asset users for the kinds they are enabled for, and by Documents\n"
"  managers for every asset\n"
"\n"
"Linking comes from ``documents_product_asset``, expiration from\n"
"``documents_compliance``, asset typing from ``asset_ledger``.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_asset_ledger_document
msgid ""
"\n"
"Documents - Asset Link\n"
"======================\n"
"\n"
"Links documents to assets (``resource.asset``).\n"
"\n"
"* documents are matched to their asset on the serial/lot number\n"
"* seeded folders per asset type: Equipment, Fleet, Machinery, Properties, with\n"
"  matching tags\n"
"* folder and tags are assigned from the asset type\n"
"* asset-specific views and filters on ``document.document``\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_document_speech
msgid ""
"\n"
"Documents - Speech\n"
"==================\n"
"\n"
"The bridge is small because the interesting half needs no code. A document's\n"
"``index_content`` is related from its attachment, and a transcript IS that\n"
"attachment's index content, so a recording becomes findable by what is said in\n"
"it through the search field Documents already had. Nothing here indexes\n"
"anything.\n"
"\n"
"What is left is the two actions a person needs: transcribe this recording, and\n"
"file this text as audio.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_document_compliance
msgid ""
"\n"
"Documents Compliance\n"
"====================\n"
"\n"
"Compliance tracking for the Documents app, per document type. The type itself,\n"
"and whether and when a document expires, belong to ``document``; this module\n"
"adds the verdict layer on top.\n"
"\n"
"* document types with default validity periods, renewal requirements and\n"
"  instructions, each scoped to the kind of record it is required of\n"
"* mandatory versus optional types\n"
"* an expiration state per document (valid, expiring soon, expired) driven by\n"
"  its date alone, and a compliance verdict per document (compliant,\n"
"  non-compliant, not applicable) driven by its type\n"
"* expiration tracking with per-type notification days (``30,7,1`` by\n"
"  default), recipients and scheduled activities\n"
"* verification and renewal from the document's details panel\n"
"* a per-entity compliance dashboard: percentage, and counts of missing,\n"
"  expired and expiring document types\n"
"\n"
"Counts exist at both levels. A document type carries totals over its own\n"
"documents, and the compliance report aggregates per entity -- partner,\n"
"employee or vehicle -- against only the mandatory types that apply to that\n"
"kind of record.\n"
"\n"
"Notifications are scheduled as activities on the document. The module sends\n"
"no email.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_document_physical
msgid ""
"\n"
"Documents Physical Originals\n"
"============================\n"
"\n"
"Tracks the whereabouts of documents whose original must be kept on file\n"
"(title deeds, promissory notes, collateral, tax documents):\n"
"\n"
"* ``stock.location`` flagged ``is_document_archive`` -- the room, cabinet,\n"
"  drawer and folder tree, with the barcode, blocking, archive-safety and\n"
"  cycle-count features the Inventory app already gives a location\n"
"* ``document.move`` -- transactional move log (intake, loan, return,\n"
"  reorganization, loss, sold)\n"
"* ``document.document`` -- ``default_location_id`` (storage location),\n"
"  ``current_location_id`` and ``custodian_partner_id`` (kept in sync by\n"
"  ``document.move``)\n"
"\n"
"Setting a Storage Location on a document is what files it: the intake move is\n"
"registered on the spot, whatever the document type. A type flagged\n"
"``requires_original`` only makes that location mandatory.\n"
"\n"
"Replaces ``document_custody``: installing this module on a database that has\n"
"it takes over its records and moves every ``document.location`` row into\n"
"``stock.location``.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_asset_ledger_document_compliance_hr
msgid ""
"\n"
"Documents Product Asset Compliance HR\n"
"=====================================\n"
"\n"
"Adds the asset manager (``hr.employee``) dimension to\n"
"``asset.compliance.report``:\n"
