#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_asset_gps_geoengine
msgid ""
"\n"
"GPS Geospatial - Product Asset / HR Bridge\n"
"==========================================\n"
"\n"
"``device_gps_geoengine`` draws what a *device* did. This adds the two other\n"
"things a person actually asks about: which vehicle it was, and who was driving.\n"
"\n"
"* the trail wizard gains its Asset/Vehicle and Operator/Driver selection modes\n"
"* ``gps.trail.result`` gains ``asset_id`` / ``operator_id`` and the display\n"
"  columns trails are named by\n"
"* ``device.client.visit`` records the vehicle and operator of each visit\n"
"* the live GPS map labels a device with its vehicle and operator\n"
"\n"
"Split out so the geospatial layer does not depend on the asset registry or on\n"
"HR. Installing map visualisation used to install both.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_device_gps
msgid ""
"\n"
"GPS Tracking - Core\n"
"===================\n"
"\n"
"GPS data collection on top of ``remote``, with no map dependency.\n"
"\n"
"* ``device.device`` extended with GPS fields and methods\n"
"* ``device.data.log.gps`` -- position points with full telemetry\n"
"* ``device.gps.data.processor`` / ``device.gps.data.validator`` -- ingestion\n"
"* vehicle telemetry: ignition, fuel, speed, engine data\n"
"* health monitoring: battery, satellites, position freshness\n"
"* route history, and an analytics report with pivot, graph and list views for\n"
"  speed, fuel consumption and device usage\n"
"\n"
"Device transport is somebody else's: ``remote`` carries HTTP and HTTPS, and a\n"
"tracker that speaks anything else needs that protocol's module installed\n"
"alongside this one. Nothing here is protocol-specific, and the demo trackers\n"
"poll an HTTP gateway so that the module depends on no transport but the base's.\n"
"Map rendering and geofencing live in ``device_gps_geoengine``.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_device_gps_geoengine
msgid ""
"\n"
"GPS Tracking - Geospatial Features\n"
"==================================\n"
"\n"
"Geospatial layer over ``device_gps``.\n"
"\n"
"* ``device.data.log.gps`` extended with a GeoPoint field, drawn on geoengine\n"
"  map views for devices and routes\n"
"* geofences (circle, polygon, rectangle) with device links, entry, exit and\n"
"  dwell alerts\n"
"* trail wizard: select by device; trails can be grouped by source, by day or\n"
"  combined. ``asset_gps_geoengine`` adds selection by asset/vehicle\n"
"  and by operator/driver, and names trails for them\n"
"* live position updates over the Odoo bus\n"
"* ``device.device`` resolves the client parcel it is currently on (within a\n"
"  configurable proximity tolerance), shown on the live GPS map\n"
"* Client Locations map: customers with GPS coordinates set in Contacts\n"
"  (Partner Assignment), on the same raster backgrounds as the live GPS map\n"
"* Every 15 minutes, a device stationary 30+ minutes off any mapped parcel\n"
"  raises a to-do: for the nearest client's salesperson if one is registered\n"
"  within 2 km, otherwise for the configured fallback (default: the sales\n"
"  lead), so the parcel gets mapped and future stops resolve on their own\n"
"* Live GPS map: optional \"Client Locations (overlay)\" layer draws each\n"
"  customer's own mapped parcel(s) when any exist, otherwise a small circle\n"
"  around their Geo Latitude/Longitude, alongside vehicles (off by default)\n"
"* Client popups (map and overlay) show the assigned salesperson\n"
"* Every 5 minutes, arrival/departure at the client parcel a device is\n"
"  currently or was most recently on is tracked and shown on the live map\n"
"* ``device.client.visit``: one row per completed (or ongoing) client visit\n"
"  -- arrival, departure, duration -- under Data & Analytics > Visitas a\n"
"  Clientes\n"
"\n"
"Requires PostGIS. This module knows about devices, points and parcels -- not\n"
"about vehicles or drivers. ``asset_gps_geoengine`` is the bridge\n"
"that teaches the map, the trails and the visits who was driving what.\n"
msgstr ""

