"    :target: https://github.com/OCA/margin-analysis/tree/19.0/account_invoice_margin_sale\n"
"    :alt: OCA/margin-analysis\n"
".. |badge4| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/weblate-Translate%20me-F47D42.png\n"
"    :target: https://translation.odoo-community.org/projects/margin-analysis-19-0/margin-analysis-19-0-account_invoice_margin_sale\n"
"    :alt: Translate me on Weblate\n"
".. |badge5| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/runboat-Try%20me-875A7B.png\n"
"    :target: https://runboat.odoo-community.org/builds?repo=OCA/margin-analysis&target_branch=19.0\n"
"    :alt: Try me on Runboat\n"
"\n"
"|badge1| |badge2| |badge3| |badge4| |badge5|\n"
"\n"
"This module makes an invoice line created from a sale order take its cost\n"
"from that order line instead of from the product, and keeps down payments\n"
"out of the margin an invoice reports.\n"
"\n"
"**Table of contents**\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"   :local:\n"
"\n"
"Installation\n"
"============\n"
"\n"
"This module is autoinstalable.\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"Once installed, the cost of every invoice line created from a sale order\n"
"is taken from the sale order line instead of from the product, and it\n"
"keeps tracking the sale order after the invoice is posted. Lines that\n"
"come from a down payment are left out of the invoice margin.\n"
"\n"
"Because the invoice line keeps tracking its sale order line, editing the\n"
"cost on the invoice does not stick: the next change to the line or its\n"
"invoice puts the sale order's figure back. Change the cost on the sale\n"
"order line instead.\n"
"\n"
"The cost is converted into the invoice's currency at the invoice date,\n"
"so an order priced in one currency can be invoiced in another and the\n"
"margin still compares two figures in the same currency.\n"
"\n"
"When an invoice line links to more than one sale order line, the cost\n"
"comes from the lowest-database-id line among those that sell the invoice\n"
"line's product. No standard invoicing flow creates that case -- the line\n"
"matcher never offers an invoice line that already carries a sale link --\n"
"so it only arises through a direct write, an import or a server action.\n"
"\n"
"If no linked sale order line sells the invoice line's product -- for\n"
"example after changing the product on a draft invoice line -- the cost\n"
"falls back to the product's, exactly as if the line had no sale source.\n"
"\n"
"The invoice margin percentage is measured against revenue **before** the\n"
"down-payment deduction, so it is not the invoice margin over its own\n"
"untaxed total. On a 1000.00 order invoiced after a 100.00 advance it\n"
"reads 50%, not the 54.76% the net revenue would give.\n"
"\n"
"The \"Show Invoice Margin\" security option hides the margin fields in the\n"
"backend views that ``account_invoice_margin`` defines; this module adds\n"
"no group and no view of its own. It is a view-level control, not a\n"
"model-level one: the fields carry no ``groups=``, so anyone who can read\n"
"the invoice line can read them through RPC, an export or a custom view.\n"
"\n"
"Bug Tracker\n"
"===========\n"
"\n"
"Bugs are tracked on `GitHub Issues <https://github.com/OCA/margin-analysis/issues>`_.\n"
"In case of trouble, please check there if your issue has already been reported.\n"
"If you spotted it first, help us to smash it by providing a detailed and welcomed\n"
"`feedback <https://github.com/OCA/margin-analysis/issues/new?body=module:%20account_invoice_margin_sale%0Aversion:%2019.0%0A%0A**Steps%20to%20reproduce**%0A-%20...%0A%0A**Current%20behavior**%0A%0A**Expected%20behavior**>`_.\n"
"\n"
"Do not contact contributors directly about support or help with technical issues.\n"
"\n"
"Credits\n"
"=======\n"
"\n"
"Authors\n"
"-------\n"
"\n"
"* AgroMarin\n"
"* Tecnativa\n"
"\n"
"Contributors\n"
